Quoting  archmage84  <archmage84@live.com>:
>From what I've gathered, you think I should stop being picky with
>artifacts, stop expecting a large number of wishes, and to play
>dwarvern lawful? Is that it?

If you want to win as soon as possible, yes. If you prefer challenge
games, maybe not. I never play with Elbereth, and resolved not to well
before ascending; but you have to acknowledge that you are reducing your
chance of ascension because you find it more elegant or satisfying.

>>Sigh. What matters isn't what you can wish up at the Castle to make
>>Gehennom very easy instead of just easy. What matters is surviving to the
>>Castle.
>It's that easy? It looks a lot harder in the spoilers...

Well, it's unfamiliar territory, but it's much the same monsters you've
been fighting so far, with the benefit of all the Stuff and wishes from
the Castle. There are one or two gotchas - like Demogorgon - but you can
be ready for those.

Of course the post-Rodney period and especially the Planes (especially Air
and Astral) can be tricky, but fundamentally that's down to unfamiliarity
and overpreparation.

I am slightly unusual, but my post-Castle record is played 23, ascended
22, lost 1. Conversely I lose lots of games pre-Castle; at my best, I was
only managing about 40% ascensions. So it's pretty clear to me that the
post-Castle game is easy. Before the Castle - if you aren't a really good
player - the game is allowed to come and kill you. After the Castle, it's
yours to throw away - now until you get the experience, you can and
probably will throw games away, but fundamentally it's an easier situation
to be in.
